.TH PROTOPEEK 1 "August 2026" "ProtoPeek 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
protopeek \- open the local ProtoPeek gRPC and HTTP workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B protopeek
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B protopeek
.RI [ options ]
.I target
.SH DESCRIPTION
ProtoPeek starts an unauthenticated local web workbench. With no target it opens
the Protocol Peek dashboard. An exact host:port connects directly to that gRPC
target. A bare host opens the dashboard's visible scan and checks only port
50051 with plaintext and port 443 with verified TLS. An HTTP(S) authority checks
its stated or default port. The gRPC, HTTP, route, scan, and roadmap surfaces are
available from the local browser interface.
.PP
The listener binds to 127.0.0.1 by default. Do not expose it to an untrusted
network. For a container published only on host loopback,
.B \-allow-non-loopback-bind
permits the container-interface listener while retaining the loopback request
Host and Origin policy. The separate
.B \-unsafe-allow-remote
option accepts non-loopback browser Hosts and requires an external TLS,
authentication, and rate-limit boundary.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-help
Print the complete command-line reference and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.B \-plaintext
Use unencrypted HTTP/2 for the target gRPC connection.
.TP
.B \-insecure
Use TLS without verifying the server certificate or name. This is not secure
and cannot be combined with
.BR \-plaintext .
.TP
.BI \-cacert " file"
Trust roots from a PEM certificate file.
.TP
.BI \-cert " file"
Present a PEM client certificate. Must be used with
.BR \-key .
.TP
.BI \-key " file"
Use the PEM private key for
.BR \-cert .
.TP
.BI \-authority " name"
Set the HTTP/2 authority and TLS verification name.
.TP
.BI \-proto " file"
Load a protobuf source file instead of relying only on reflection. May be
specified more than once.
.TP
.BI \-protoset " file"
Load an encoded FileDescriptorSet. May be specified more than once.
.TP
.BI \-import-path " directory"
Add a protobuf import directory.
.TP
.BI \-H " name:value"
Add metadata to reflection and RPC requests. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-rpc-header " name:value"
Add metadata only to RPC invocations.
.TP
.BI \-reflect-header " name:value"
Add metadata only to reflection requests.
.TP
.BI \-connect-timeout " seconds"
Limit initial connection time.
.TP
.BI \-max-time " seconds"
Set the ProtoPeek-owned local wall for one ordinary RPC invocation. When the
wall is reached, return bounded partial evidence without presenting local
cancellation as a server gRPC status. Zero or a value above 60 seconds uses the
built-in 60-second safety wall.
.TP
.BI \-bind " address"
Bind the browser listener. Defaults to 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B \-allow-non-loopback-bind
Permit a non-loopback container listener while still accepting browser
requests only for loopback Hosts and matching Origins. Use only when the outer
container port is published on host loopback.
.TP
.BI \-port " port"
Choose the browser listener port. Zero selects an available port.
.TP
.BI \-open-browser= bool
Enable or disable automatic browser opening.
.TP
.B \-unsafe-allow-remote
Permit a non-loopback browser listener and accept non-loopback browser Hosts.
The listener has no built-in user authentication; use only behind an explicit
TLS, authentication, and rate-limit boundary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open the Protocol Peek dashboard:
.B protopeek
.TP
Probe the bounded candidates for a bare host in the visible scan:
.B protopeek localhost
.TP
Connect to a plaintext local gRPC server:
.B protopeek \-plaintext localhost:50051
.TP
Start without opening a browser:
.B protopeek \-open-browser=false
.SH STATE
Saved targets, requests, and workspace settings are stored in the local browser
profile. Automatic history and default exports redact known credential fields,
but exported debugging data should still be reviewed before sharing.
.SH ALIAS
.B pp
is an identical executable entrypoint. If another program already owns that
name, use
.B protopeek
instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pp (1),
the project documentation at https://protopeek.shreyam1008.com.np/docs/
